# Docs before commit

If the user asks for a commit (or you are committing), review staged changes and update **only what changed**:

| File | When |
|------|------|
| `docs/architecture.md` | New modules, flows, layout, ports |
| `docs/features/<area>.md` | Features and UI surfaces for that area |
| `docs/features/api-reference.md` | New / changed HTTP endpoints |
| `docs/features/data-models.md` | New tables / columns / schemas |
| `docs/features/configuration.md` | New or changed `STOCK_*` / env vars |
| `docs/design-system.md` | Shared SCSS tokens, patterns, or design-system file layout |
| `docs/developer/setup.md` | Dev workflow, Alembic, Postgres setup |
| `docs/operations/docker.md` | Compose services, ports, volumes |

`docs/functionalities.md` is the routing index — only edit when adding or removing a feature page.

## Verify before commit

If staged changes touch `docs/**`, `mkdocs.yml`, or `docs/requirements.txt`, run before committing:

```bash
pip install -r docs/requirements.txt
mkdocs build --strict --site-dir _site
```

Stage doc updates with the code commit.
